---
const vowels = [
  ["begin", "began", "begun", "The concert began at 7."],
  ["drink", "drank", "drunk", "He has drunk all the milk."],
  ["sing", "sang", "sung", "They sang beautifully."],
  ["ring", "rang", "rung", "The bell has rung."],
  ["swim", "swam", "swum", "She has swum across the pool."]
];
const mixed = [
  ["go", "went", "gone", "He has gone home."],
  ["see", "saw", "seen", "I have seen that film."],
  ["eat", "ate", "eaten", "She has eaten lunch."],
  ["break", "broke", "broken", "He broke his pencil."],
  ["write", "wrote", "written", "I have written a letter."]
];
---

<div class="topic-sheet">
  <h1>Irregular Verbs - Vowel changes</h1>
  <section class="summary-block summary-peach">
    <h2>The middle vowel changes</h2>
    <table class="punct-table summary-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th class="th-feature" scope="col">Base</th>
          <th class="th-example" scope="col">Past</th>
          <th class="th-rule" scope="col">Past participle</th>
          <th class="th-function" scope="col">Example</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          vowels.map(([base, past, participle, example]) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">{base}</th>
              <td>{past}</td>
              <td>{participle}</td>
              <td>{example}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>The usual pattern is <strong>i → a → u</strong>: <em>drink → drank → drunk, sing → sang → sung, begin → began → begun</em>. Say them as a rhythm: <em>sing–sang–sung, ring–rang–rung</em>.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="summary-block summary-lilac">
    <h2>No fixed pattern</h2>
    <table class="punct-table summary-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th class="th-feature" scope="col">Base</th>
          <th class="th-example" scope="col">Past</th>
          <th class="th-rule" scope="col">Past participle</th>
          <th class="th-function" scope="col">Example</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          mixed.map(([base, past, participle, example]) => (
            <tr>
              <th scope="row">{base}</th>
              <td>{past}</td>
              <td>{participle}</td>
              <td>{example}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>These need memorising. There is no single rule that builds <em>go → went → gone</em>.</p>
  </section>
</div>
